\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 7.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls17\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 AI stop-trespassing behavior is improved
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 8.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls18\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Boats/Undersea Tunnels pathing problem fixed
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 9.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls19\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Can continue play when someone wins the alien endgame
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 10.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls20\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Autocentering on special attacks now happens correctly
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 11.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls21\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Chat window scrolling bug fixed.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 12.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls22\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Tile Improvement placement precision increased.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Advanced User Notes:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls23\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
How to make a Call to Power Scenario Pack
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls24\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 /demo, /attach, /detach, and /rnd options
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls25\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 AI taking over PBEM/Hotseat Player
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls26\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Registry location for .csg files (Call to Power Saved Game files)
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 5.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls27\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Adding Governments in Scenarios
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Readme Miscellanea:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls28\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
In PBEM and Hotseat Games, you may wish to turn off auto-turn cycling if you find it disconcerting that your last unit movement will end your turn and either ask you to mail the saved game or call the next player, depending on what type of game.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls29\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 To load
 a saved Hotseat game, you must go to the Single Player screen, and load the game there, even though a hot seat game is technically a multi-player game.  
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls30\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 When saving a Hotseat game, you\rquote 
ll find that the default saved game name comes from Player 1, even if it\rquote s Player 5 that saves, for instance.  Do not be alarmed, simply name the game however you want and accept that Player 1\rquote 
s name will be used as the default for saving Hotseat games.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls31\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 You may only load PBEM games by double-clicking on the PBEM game\rquote 
s icon.  This will find and launch Civilization: Call to Power.  If the saved game file, \'93*.csg\'94 doesn\rquote 
t launch Civilization: Call to Power, run Civilization: Call to Power once, and then quit.  The act of running the game will install the necessary registry entry to map \'93*.csg\'94 files correctly.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 5.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls32\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
You can play a single-player game as a color other than Blue (the default player 1 color) if you like.  Set up a Hotseat game, with all players other than you set to be Computer players.  Simply put yourself in a
 player slot other than the first one, and you\rquote ll be the appropriate color for that game.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 6.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls33\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
New keyboard shortcuts were added with version 1.2, so you must remove your custom key mappings if you want to use the new keyboard shortcuts.  This is easily done; simply open up the folder that contains CivCTP.exe (most likely c:\\Program Files\\
Activision\\Civilization-Call to Power\\ctp_program\\ctp) and delete the file called \'93userkeymap.txt.\'94  If you do this, be aware that you\rquote ll lose any custom key mappings that you set up, if you manually configured the keyboard previously.

\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 {\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1026{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}
{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLine}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}\picscalex864\picscaley6\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0
\picw1764\pich882\picwgoal1000\pichgoal500\wmetafile8\bliptag945835045\blipupi1439{\*\blipuid 38604c255eab1257935c4a96b77d293c}010009000003310000000000070000000000050000000b0200000000050000000c02f401e803070000001b04f401e80300000000050000001402000000000500
00001302f401e803050000001402f40100000500000013020000a005e80300000000430000000000}}{
\par New Features:
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs20 Hot Seat}{\fs20  
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
This is the ability to play a multiplayer game on a single computer by alternating turns at the keyboard. 
\par To start a hotseat game: 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls34\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
Click the Hot Seat button on the Initial Play Screen, and you'll be taken to the Single Player New Game Screen.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls35\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
Set whatever game options that you want on the Initial Play Screen as if you were setting up a normal single-player game.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls36\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Launch Game
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls37\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
You'll be prompted to enter some information about the hotseat game with the Hot Seat/PBEM Interface Screen.\~ You'll want to pick the Civilizations for the various players, and whether they're AI players or Human players.\~
 You can also enter a name for each player.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 Once launched, the game will allow each player to play their turn, and when they end their turn, the screen will be blanked, and the user will be told whose turn it is.\~
 This next player then will presumably sit at the computer, press OK, play their turn, and so on.\~ Between each player, the screen will be blanked, and a message will be given indicating whose turn is next. 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 This game can be saved at any time, and, when loaded, will resume hotseat-style play. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Play by E-mail (PBEM)}{\fs20  
\par This feature provides the ability to play games of CTP via email.\~ That is, each player plays their turn, emails a file to the next player in the game, which they then load, play and pass on, etc. 
\par To start a PBEM game: 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls38\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
Click the Play Email Game button on the Initial Play Screen, and you'll be taken to the Single Player New Game Screen.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls39\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
Set whatever game options you want on this Initial Play Screen as if you were setting up a normal single player game.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls40\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Launch game
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls41\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 You'll be prompted to enter some information 
about the PBEM game by the Hot Seat/PBEM Interface Screen.\~ You'll want to pick the Civilizations for the various players, and whether they're AI players or Human players.\~
 You also need to enter the name for each player, and an email address for each player.\~ These email addresses are used to help the players pass the PBEM saved game file around.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 When the game is finished loading, you'll be able to play one turn, and then the screen will blank and you'll receive a message telling you to email the saved gam
e file to the next player in the chain.\~ The save file will be saved automatically to your Windows desktop and will be named:\~
 CTP_Email_To_********.csg, where the ****** corresponds to the email address of the person who should get the file next, and the current turn number.  For example:  \'93CTP_Email_To_joe@hostname.com(Turn_50).csg.\'94\~
 It's then the user's responsibility to send this file to the right person.\~ The email address used here is the email address entered into the Hot Seat/PBEM Interface Screen. 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 To continue a PBEM game: 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls42\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
Once you've received a PBEM game file from a game in progress, you continue playing by double-clicking that icon from Windows Explorer.\~ The file can reside anywhere on your hard drive.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls43\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
By double-clicking it, you will launch Call to Power, and it will load the PBEM saved game and let you play your turn.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls44\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
When you're done with your turn, and you press End Turn (or hit 'n,') it will blank the screen and save the file out to the Windows Desktop.\~
 The file will be named as before, with the email address of the next recipient in the PBEM game and the current turn number as parts of the filename.\~ It's then the user's responsibility to mail this file to the appropriate person.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\i\fs20 IMPORTANT\~}{\fs20  To accomplish this, auto-launch by double-clicking on the save file. Call to Power must modify the Windows registry.\~
 It does this the first time you launch version 1.2 of Call to Power, so therefore you won't be able to play a saved PBEM game until you've run version 1.2 of Call to Power at least once.\~
 Before attempting to participate in a PBEM game, make sure that you've launched the version 1.2 executable and quit back to Windows.\~ This will ensure proper PBEM save file launching. 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs20 Hotseat/PBEM Interface Screen}{\fs20  
\par This screen is used in the game setup sequences for both Hot Seat and PBEM games.\~ Its primary function is to allow you to enter information about each of the players in the game.\~ It's divided into 4 columns: 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls45\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 Civilization
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls46\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Human or AI
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls47\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Player Name
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls48\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Player Email Address (only used for PBEM games)
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 Column 1 is the Civilization.\~ This is which Civ the player is going to play.\~
 There may be restrictions on which Civ the player can play depending on what type of game is being launched (a scenario may lock the Civs so that they can't be changed.)\~
 Clicking on the button in the Civilization column alternates between legal Civs for that player. \line Column 2 toggles between Human and AI when the button is pressed.\~ You can assign human players to the game by toggling this to "Human."\~
 Once toggled to "Human" you can then enter a player name and email address (for PBEM games.) \line Column 3 is the name of the player, and can only be edited when the player is Human. \line Column 4 is the email address of the player, 
and can only be edited when the player is Human, and the game being played is a PBEM game. 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 When all of the settings are to the user's liking, pressing Close accepts them. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Scenario Pack Interface}{\fs20  
\par On the Single Player - New Game Screen, there's a new button:\~ "Select Scenario," which you may pick as one of the game setup options.\~ This will bring up the Scenario Pack Interface Screen and allow you to select a scenario to play. 
\par You'll see the message "Please select the Scenario Pack you wish to use."\~ Scenarios are organized into individual scenario packs, and any number of scenario packs can be installed at any time.\~
 You can select a Scenario Pack by either double-clicking on its entry in the list, or by single-clicking on its entry in the list and pressing the OK button. 
\par This will take you to the list of Scenarios found in that Scenario Pack. 
\par You'll see the message "Please choose which Scenario you are interested in playing." and will be allowed to pick the scenario.\~ You can either double-click it, or click it and press OK. 
\par At this point, depending on what kind of scenario it is, the game will either launch, or you'll be returned to the Single Player - New Game Screen to be allowed to set some game options. 
\par In the first case, the scenario has an associated save file (either a saved scenario game, or a saved scenario map) and you'll be launched into the game init process. 
\par In the second case, the scenario does NOT have an associated save file (scenario game, or scenario map) and will take place on a random map.\~
 When you're returned to the Single Player New Game Screen, you'll notice that beneath the "Select Scenario" button (which is now called "Standard Game") the name of the Scenario will be indicated.\~ If you decide that you no longer wish you p
lay this scenario, pressing the Standard Game button will make it a standard, non-scenario game. 
\par }{\b\fs20 New Scenario Options}{\fs20  
\par There are now several new scenario options with the 1.2 version of Call to Power. 
\par Previously, we offered the following types of scenario games: 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard\plain \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls49\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 
Saved Scenario Map with starting locations for each player where the player could play as any Civ when launching a new scenario game.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls50\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
Saved Scenario Map with starting locations for each player where the player had to play the Civs that were saved with the map.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls51\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
Saved Scenario Map with starting locations for any number of Civilizations, where the player had to play one of those Civilizations on that map.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls52\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Saved Scenario Games where the user had to play as whatever civilization player 1 wa
s playing.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 Now, we've added several new types of scenario games: 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls53\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 
Saved Scenario Games where the user can play as any of the players that were saved in the game.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\tx720\faauto\ls54\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\fs20 Random Map games, where the scenario can use modified data files, graphics, sprites, and
 so forth.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 We also now offer the user the ability to choose the difficulty and level of Barbarian activity when they launch a saved scenario game. 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 With these additions, we now have a much more well-rounded feature set for scenarios.\~
 Note that any of these types of scenario games can be played as Single Player, Hot Seat, Play by Email, or Multiplayer games. 
\par }{\b\fs20 New Suite of Build Queue Messages}{\fs20  
\par First, you get messages when Improvements are finished building.\~ These are identified by a new Improvements icon, which looks like a couple of buildings with a green halo around them. 
\par Now, when a Unit, Improvement, or Wonder is built, you'll receive a message indicating what was just built, and what's next in the queue (and is now building.)\~ If the queue is empty, you'll be told that the queue is empty. 
\par We provided this feature to allow you to keep better tabs on your cities.\~ Simply indicating that the queue is empty was not nearly enough information. 
\par }{\b\fs20 City Screen Now Has a Turns To Next Pop Display}{\fs20  
\par We removed the food readout from the City Screen as it wasn't really providing very useful information in the context of the City Screen, and replaced it with a "Turns to Next Pop" indicator, which shows you the number of turns that must pass befor
e the selected city will increase in size again. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Trade Routes Can Be Toggled On and Off}{\fs20  
\par You can now turn the display of Trade Routes on and off via a keyboard shortcut.\~ This feature is provided to reduce the amount of visual clutter in the game when there are a lot of trade routes established.\~
 To toggle the display of trade routes, press the double-quotes key ("). Hold down the shift key, and press the \lquote  (quote) key.
\par }{\b\fs20 Message Eyepoints Can Be Activated From The Keyboard}{\fs20  
\par For dropdown messages that have an Eyepoint, you can now press the ctrl-y (control lowercase Y) instead of clicking on the Eyepoint, and the Eyepoint will activate.\~ 
\par }{\b\fs20 Message Indicating What City Slaves Were Sent To}{\fs20  
\par After successfully enslaving someone, you will receive an indication as to which city the slaves were placed in.\~ Before, it was ambiguous as to where the slaves went. 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 {\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1027{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}
{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLine}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}\picscalex864\picscaley6\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0
\picw1764\pich882\picwgoal1000\pichgoal500\wmetafile8\bliptag-2026653276\blipupi1439{\*\blipuid 8733b9a4c20470093df6f2ae9249556e}
010009000003310000000000070000000000050000000b0200000000050000000c02f401e803070000001b04f401e8030000000005000000140200000000050000001302f401e803050000001402f40100000500000013020000a005e80300000000000000000000}}{
\par Bug Fixes:
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\b\fs20 Graphics Freeze From Double-Clicking an Advance to Research.}{\fs20  
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 Introduced with version 1.1 was a "graphics freeze" where units would display in the incorrect locations.
\~ This happened when you selected the next advance to research on the pop up Research Screen by double-clicking the desired resource.\~ This has been fixed for version 1.2. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Trading with AI Bug Fixed}{\fs20  
\par If you offer goods for sale, and the AI agrees to buy them, the route will now be created correctly. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Captured Cities Get Selected}{\fs20  
\par Right after you successfully capture a city, we now select the city so that you can immediately edit it.\~ It's more of a convenience thing than a bug fix. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Fixed Eyepoint Click Centering And City Selection in Some Messages}{\fs20  
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li720\ri720\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin720\lin720\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 The internal names of these messages are:
\par 32CrisisStarvingCities \endash  Indication that your city is starving.\line 37CityQueueIsEmpty \endash  The build queue is empty in the city.\line 100CityRioting \endash  Your city is rioting\line 23IACityWillStarve \endash 
 Your city is about to starve by one population unit.\line 159InjunctionCompleteVictim \endash  You\rquote ve been the victim of an Injunction\line 161SueCompleteVictim \endash  Someone has successfully sued you\line 250UnitGainedVeteranStatus \endash 
 One of you units is now a veteran unit. \line 106CantBuildUnitCellIsFull \endash  You can\rquote t build a unit because you already have 9 units in your city.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\fs20 Fixed CD-check requirement for all players in a multiplayer game.}{\fs20  
\par }\pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 This bug was introduced with version 1.1 and has been corrected.\~
 You may now play a multiplayer game as long as at least one player has the CD. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Fixed Hardcoded "Reset Trade Route" String}{\fs20  
\par This string was causing problems in non-English versions of Call to Power. 
\par }{\b\fs20 AI Stop-Trespassing Behavior Is Improved}{\fs20  
\par The AI will preferentially path around land owned by a player with which the AI has a stop-trespassing agreement.\~ It should be noted, however, that only land that has had a worker placed on it (no matter how briefly) will be marked as owned.\~
 The AI also still violates trespassing agreements by walking through owned choke points if there is un-owned land on the other side and no other way around. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Boats/Undersea Tunnels Pathing Problem Fixed}{\fs20  
\par Boats would use the undersea tunnels when travelling, even though they shouldn't have had access to them while at sea. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Can Continue Play When Someone Wins The Alien Endgame}{\fs20  
\par We now offer the option to continue playing even if someone has won via the Alien Endgame. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Autocentering On Special Attacks Now Happens Correctly}{\fs20  
\par Combat autocentering wasn't occuring when enemy units performed a special attack.\~ This has been fixed. 
\par }{\b\fs20 Chat Window Scrolling Bug Fixed}{\fs20  
\par The chat window, which was broken in 1.0, was "fixed" in 1.1 to not exhibit the double-triple-quadruple-spacing problem, but was broken in its own right, eating lines and not displaying them correctly.\~
 Now, in 1.2, it's fixed again, only this time, correctly.\~ :-\} 
\par }{\b\fs20 Tile Improvement Placement Precision Increased}{\fs20  
\par It was sometimes difficult to place Tile Improvements, as they would end up adjacent to the tile that was intended.\~ This has been fixed. \line \~ 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel1\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\fs36\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\fs20 {\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1028{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}
{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLine}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}\picscalex864\picscaley6\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0
